1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,040
evening, because Monday means going back to a job that's quietly crushing you.

2
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:05,120
I remember sitting in my car after work one evening, engine still running, staring at

3
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:10,400
the steering wheel, because I couldn't make myself go upstairs yet.

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:15,920
The job itself wasn't even the worst part, it was feeling constantly reduced by someone

5
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:21,640
above me, every conversation felt like I was becoming smaller, I called my parents hoping

6
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:27,840
someone would finally say, this isn't normal, you're burning out, instead I got practical

7
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:34,280
advice, find another job before quitting this one, rational advice, responsible advice,

8
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:39,640
but what I actually needed in that moment was someone to hear the human being underneath

9
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:46,200
the problem, the gap between what we need and what we are trained to give each other
